egin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -13 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -13 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -13 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -13 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & -13 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3w &=6 \\\\ y-3w &=-5 \\\\ z+2w &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3w+6 \\\\ y &=3w-5 \\\\ z &=-2w+3 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3w+6 \\\\ 3w-5 \\\\ -2w+3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557549 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a654292-8518-53cd-98bb-71caefcd0a07" :answer/type 